    "introduction": "Coca-Cola HBC produces, packages and distributes beverages across a range of European and emerging markets, including Nigeria. As a bottling partner, it handles local manufacturing, logistics and customer relationships for Coca-Cola products alongside other drinks in its portfolio. Customers include supermarkets, convenience stores, restaurants and hospitality operators. Revenue comes from beverage sales, with volumes, pricing and the mix of pack sizes and products influencing results. Its role is operationally different from owning the Coca-Cola brand itself. Production efficiency, distribution reach and retail execution matter, while weather, consumer spending, packaging costs and local market conditions can change demand and margins.",
